{"content":{"blocks":[{"caller":{"type":"direct"},"id":"toolu_01UUL4VtPJWFaaK1p8WPgVHc","input":{"command":"gh pr create --base main --head fix/opencode-continuation --title \"opencode: make bridged sessions continuable (re-target of #8 to main)\" --body \"$(cat <<'EOF'\n#8 was merged into `docs/fabrication-tiers-and-opencode-provider-bug` rather than `main`, and did not auto-retarget because that base branch still existed when #7 merged. So commit `7737549` — the entire opencode fix — is **not on main**. This PR lands it.\n\nContent is identical to #8; #7's docs commit is already on main, so the delta here is exactly the one fix commit.\n\n## The bug\n\nA fabricated opencode session rendered perfectly and could not be talked to. Three defects, each invisible on screen.\n\n1. **`providerID` was a provenance value in a dispatch field.** The adapter wrote `providerID: \"turnbridge\"`. opencode resolves its agent loop's model from what the session stores — not `-m`, not the TUI model picker — so it threw `ProviderModelNotFoundError` and exited at step 0 without issuing a request. Under a registered project that surfaced as exit 0 with empty output and a TUI that silently swallowed the prompt; under `global`, as `UnknownError`. Now resolved against `opencode models`: kept verbatim when opencode can run it, otherwise substituted and disclosed in the import notice and a launch note; refuses to fabricate (falls back to bootstrap) when nothing is listed.\n\n2. **Ids are an ordering key.** Parts render in `id` order, so random uuid part ids put `step-finish` before `step-start` once assistant messages gained step parts. Native message ids are time-ascending base62 in the `f` range, and `msg_tb_<uuid>` sorts after them — every fabricated message ranked after the reply opencode was about to write. A resumed session answered and then kept generating, 10–13 turns for one prompt, against a native control that answered once in 12.6s. Ids are now minted in emission order.\n\n3. **Native part shape.** Assistant messages are wrapped in `step-start … step-finish` now, with the launch repo's `HEAD` as `snapshot`. The spec's \"not required\" verdict had been reached by checking rendering, which was the wrong test.\n\n## Verification\n\nEnd to end against opencode 1.18.5: a 4-turn Claude Code conversation bridged into opencode answers a question about its own history — exit 0, 25s, one assistant turn, correct marker. Native controls before and after. `-m` overrides the stored model again.\n\n91 tests pass (was 88). One rewritten — it had asserted `providerID === \"turnbridge\"`, so the suite was defending the bug.\n\n## Still open\n\nThe two opencode probes, and codex 0.147.0 drift.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01XvcBwjacvqTAFGdaMhEcei\nEOF\n)\" 2>&1 | tail -3","description":"Open PR retargeting fix to main","timeout":180000},"name":"Bash","type":"tool_use"}],"role":"assistant"},"context":{"branch":"fix/opencode-continuation","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/turnbridge","head":"77375496d5ae42be257ec16d189b3204a09dd681","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/turnbridge.git"},"id":"ev2-0e70d1c07ffc7ca37ae37c90fdda59a47aa9ecdc11ec25c2f3949479ddd05094","kind":"conversation_turn","meta":{"actor":{"id":"claude-opus-5","type":"agent"},"model":"claude-opus-5","session_id":"4fc5e727-a1d5-4399-a448-9d24a0ce9c15","source":"claude-code","source_version":"2.1.227"},"occurred_at":"2026-08-11T12:46:53.715Z","producer":{"tool":"cledger","version":"0.20.0"},"raw":{"data":{"cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/turnbridge","effort":"high","entrypoint":"cli","gitBranch":"fix/opencode-continuation","isSidechain":false,"message":{"content":[{"caller":{"type":"direct"},"id":"toolu_01UUL4VtPJWFaaK1p8WPgVHc","input":{"command":"gh pr create --base main --head fix/opencode-continuation --title \"opencode: make bridged sessions continuable (re-target of #8 to main)\" --body \"$(cat <<'EOF'\n#