{"content":{"blocks":[{"caller":{"type":"direct"},"id":"toolu_01VJoCekjWen7RdajfUYgkmb","input":{"command":"git add -A && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\nopencode: make bridged sessions continuable\n\nA fabricated opencode session rendered perfectly and could not be talked to.\nThree defects, each invisible on screen, found by asking a resumed session to\nrecall a marker planted in its bridged history.\n\n1. providerID. The adapter wrote `providerID: \"turnbridge\"` per the old\n   contract rule to never substitute a recognized-but-false model id. opencode\n   resolves its agent loop's model from what the session stores — not from -m,\n   not from the TUI model picker — so it threw ProviderModelNotFoundError and\n   exited at step 0 without issuing a request. Symptoms varied by scoping: under\n   a registered project `opencode run -s` exited 0 with empty output and the TUI\n   silently swallowed the prompt; under `global` it surfaced as UnknownError.\n   Now the source model is resolved against `opencode models` and kept verbatim\n   when opencode can run it, otherwise substituted and disclosed in the import\n   notice and a launch note. With nothing listed, fabrication refuses and falls\n   back to bootstrap rather than writing a session that cannot dispatch.\n\n2. Ids are an ordering key. Parts render in `id` order, so `prt_tb_<uuid>`\n   scrambled them the moment assistant messages gained step-start/step-finish —\n   exports showed step-finish ahead of step-start. Worse, native message ids are\n   time-ascending base62 currently in the `f` range, and `msg_tb_<uuid>` sorts\n   after them: every fabricated message ranked after the reply opencode was\n   about to write. A resumed session then answered and kept generating, 10-13\n   assistant turns for one prompt, where a native session in the same directory,\n   project and model answered once in 12.6s. Ids are now minted in emission\n   order, with message ids below anything opencode will mint next.\n\n3. Native part shape. Assistant messages carried a bare `text` part; native ones\n   are wrapped in step-start … step-finish. The spec called step-start \"not\n   required\" on the strength of rendering, which was the wrong test. Emitted\n   now, with the launch repo's HEAD as `snapshot`.\n\nVerified end to end against opencode 1.18.5: a 4-turn Claude Code conversation\nbridged into opencode answers a question about its own history, exit 0 in 25s,\none assistant turn. `-m` also overrides the stored model again, which it could\nnot do while the provider was unresolvable.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01XvcBwjacvqTAFGdaMhEcei\nEOF\ngit log --oneline -2; git status --short; echo \"(clean if blank)\"","description":"Commit the fix"},"name":"Bash","type":"tool_use"}],"role":"assistant"},"context":{"branch":"fix/opencode-continuation","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/turnbridge","head":"77375496d5ae42be257ec16d189b3204a09dd681","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/turnbridge.git"},"id":"ev2-07d3d47bf048fd2b2e513dc9f93f5d8b2b46f653b31b978b38b92ab93158fcf5","kind":"conversation_turn","meta":{"actor":{"id":"claude-opus-5","type":"agent"},"model":"claude-opus-5","session_id":"4fc5e727-a1d5-4399-a448-9d24a0ce9c15","source":"claude-code","source_version":"2.1.227"},"occurred_at":"2026-08-11T11:42:06.952Z","producer":{"tool":"cledger","version":"0.20.0"},"raw":{"data":{"cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/turnbridge","effort":"high","entrypoint":"cli","gitBranch":"fix/opencode-continuation","isSidechain":false,"message":{"content":[{"caller":{"type":"direct"},"id":"toolu_01VJoCekjWen7RdajfUYgkmb","input":{"command":"git add -A && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\nopencode: make bridged sessions continuable\n\nA fabricated opencode session rendered perfectly and could not be talked to.\nThree defects, each invisible on screen, found by asking a resumed session to\nrecall a marker planted in its brid