{"content":{"blocks":[{"caller":{"type":"direct"},"id":"toolu_01XFqHVkdyysSesscC2bA35K","input":{"file_path":"/Users/evintunador/.claude/projects/-Users-evintunador-repos-evintunador-turnbridge/memory/turnbridge-mvp-decisions.md","new_string":"  *Fixed 2026-08-06 in PR #8 (stacked on docs PR #7, both unmerged).* The\n  runaway regeneration turned out to be a **second** defect, not the model:\n  **opencode treats ids as an ordering key.** Parts render in `id` order (so\n  random `prt_tb_<uuid>` put `step-finish` before `step-start` once assistant\n  messages gained step parts), and native message ids are time-ascending base62\n  in the `f` range — `msg_tb_<uuid>` sorts *after* them, so every fabricated\n  message ranked after the reply opencode was about to write. Result: a resumed\n  session answered then kept generating (10-13 turns for one prompt) where a\n  native session answered once in 12.6s. Ids are now minted in emission order\n  with message ids below anything opencode mints next. Verified end to end:\n  bridged 4-turn conversation answers about its own history, exit 0, 25s, one\n  assistant turn. Generalizable lesson for new targets: **check whether the\n  target orders by id anywhere**, and never conclude from rendering alone —\n  all three defects here rendered perfectly.","old_string":"  Unconfirmed side observation: after the fix the run answered then regenerated\n  ~237 times until killed — possibly a weak free model, possibly the missing\n  `step-start`/`step-finish` parts on fabricated assistant messages.","replace_all":false},"name":"Edit","type":"tool_use"}],"role":"assistant"},"context":{"branch":"fix/opencode-continuation","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/turnbridge","head":"77375496d5ae42be257ec16d189b3204a09dd681","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/turnbridge.git"},"id":"ev2-bf0219ab2c64bcdb607b0a3a782f814d4b9108e4ec0670d7b22b306e98207fa0","kind":"conversation_turn","meta":{"actor":{"id":"claude-opus-5","type":"agent"},"model":"clau