{"content":{"blocks":[{"text":"Fixed and verified end to end. It was **three** defects, not one — and the two I hadn't found yet were the reason my earlier \"one wrong string\" diagnosis was incomplete.\n\n**1. `providerID`** — as diagnosed. Resolved against `opencode models` now: kept verbatim when opencode can run it, otherwise substituted and disclosed in the import notice *and* a launch note. If nothing is listed, fabrication refuses and falls back to bootstrap rather than writing a session that can't dispatch.\n\n**2. Ids are an ordering key** — this was the real cause of the runaway I'd written off as \"possibly a weak model.\"\n- Parts render in **`id` order**, so random uuid part ids scrambled them the instant assistant messages gained step parts (`step-finish` exported ahead of `step-start`). Invisible before, because messages had exactly one part.\n- Native message ids are time-ascending base62 in the `f` range; `msg_tb_<uuid>` sorts *after* them, so every fabricated message ranked after the reply opencode was about to write. A resumed session answered and then kept generating — 10–13 turns for one prompt, against a native control that answered once in 12.6s.\n\n**3. Native part shape** — `step-start … step-finish` now emitted, with the repo's `HEAD` as `snapshot`. Your point 2 was exactly right, and the spec's \"not required\" verdict was reached by checking rendering, which was the wrong test.\n\n**Verified:** a 4-turn Claude Code conversation bridged into opencode answers a question about its own history — exit 0, 25s, one assistant turn, correct marker. Native controls run before and after. `-m` overrides the stored model again, so turnbridge's pick is just a starting default.\n\nTests 88 → 91. One rewritten: it had asserted `providerID === \"turnbridge\"`, so the suite was actively defending the bug.\n\nTwo corrections to things I told you earlier: the runaway was ours, not the model — I flagged it as \"possibly just a weak free model\" and that was wrong. And my \"fix is one string\" framing understated it; the provider fix alone still left a session that ran away.\n\n**PR #8** is pushed, stacked on #7. Merge #7 first and #8 retargets to main automatically. All test debris cleaned up — zero `ses_tb_` sessions, zero import files, working tree clean.\n\nStill open, untouched: the two probes, and codex 0.147.0 drift.\n\nresult: Fixed opencode continuation end to end — three defects (unresolvable `providerID`, id-based ordering for both parts and messages, missing native step parts); a bridged 4-turn conversation now answers about its own history in 25s with one assistant turn, 91/91 tests, shipped as stacked PR #8 on top of docs PR #7.","type":"text"}],"role":"assistant"},"context":{"branch":"fix/opencode-continuation","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/turnbridge","head":"77375496d5ae42be257ec16d189b3204a09dd681","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/turnbridge.git"},"id":"ev2-4a11cfc9d6f6ac8588b83e1efdbe832364b4b64586909fa1a34ff6d258ba155c","kind":"conversation_turn","meta":{"actor":{"id":"claude-opus-5","type":"agent"},"model":"claude-opus-5","session_id":"4fc5e727-a1d5-4399-a448-9d24a0ce9c15","source":"claude-code","source_version":"2.1.227"},"occurred_at":"2026-08-11T11:42:58.815Z","producer":{"tool":"cledger","version":"0.20.0"},"raw":{"data":{"cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/turnbridge","effort":"high","entrypoint":"cli","gitBranch":"fix/opencode-continuation","isSidechain":false,"message":{"content":[{"text":"Fixed and verified end to end. It was **three** defects, not one — and the two I hadn't found yet were the reason my earlier \"one wrong string\" diagnosis was incomplete.\n\n**1. `providerID`** — as diagnosed. Resolved against `opencode models` now: kept verbatim when opencode can run it, otherwise substituted and disclosed in the import notice *and* a launch note. If nothing is listed, fabrication refuses and falls back to bootstrap rather than writing a session that can't dispatch.